Print two lines, each the result of one regular-expression rewrite, printed
with `.` followed by `cr`.

1. In the string `due 2026-01-31 and 2025-12-01`, rewrite every date from
   YYYY-MM-DD to DD/MM/YYYY, leaving the rest of the text alone.

2. This string has leading and trailing spaces and runs of whitespace inside
   it, including a newline:

       "  a   b
        c  "

   Strip the leading and trailing whitespace, then collapse every remaining
   run of whitespace to a single space.
